    {
      "id": "wavre-prussian-iii-corps",
      "nationId": "prussians-1815",
      "name": "Thielemann's III Corps",
      "formation": "III Corps, Army of the Lower Rhine",
      "side": "Prussian",
      "summary": "Left behind as Blücher's rearguard while the rest of the army marched to Waterloo. Kemphen's brigade held Wavre's bridges against Vandamme, Luck's Landwehr the Dyle beside it, and Stülpnagel's the upstream crossings at Bierges and Limale, where Grouchy turned the flank on the 19th.",
      "notes": [
        "Luck's brigade was all Landwehr, two Kurmark regiments, where the list's brigade needs a Line regiment, which shows as a historical departure.",
        "Borcke's brigade had begun the march to Waterloo and only part of it came back to fight.",
        "A Prussian brigade was the size of another army's division, so the whole corps is here. Take the brigades you want; each is a force in itself.",
        "Each regiment's three battalions are the list's two Musketeer and one Fusilier battalions, or three Landwehr. The corps' cavalry and reserve artillery aren't included, and the order of battle doesn't number the brigades' foot batteries.",
        "Thielemann commands as the optional Corps Commander (Albion Triumphant p. 78), at Staff Rating 8; his brigade commanders at 8, the list's lowest. Our judgement."
      ],
